      {
        "id": 224983,
        "name": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "username": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/{size}/1869_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-01-10T03:15:18.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>This is more of what I was referencing:&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Danse_macabre_(Saint-Sa%C3%ABns)\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Danse Macabre, by Saint-Saens.</a></p>\n<p>I see now what you were going for with the pun, but... maybe workshop it a bit.&nbsp; Maybe it's me, but I don't tend to associate the word Dense with a horde of things. A block of lead is dense; a throng of zombies is more... swarming, shifting, almost amorphous.&nbsp; It almost implies fluidity to me, not density.&nbsp; But hey, ymmv.</p>",
